  (text "Model 6G6-B — Blonde Bassman-style · Circuit Codex · CC-BY-SA 4.0 · redrawn from circuit facts" (at 20 12 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2)) (justify left)) (uuid "370820a2-1951-4f4c-b1e3-81d0afedbfa4"))
  (text "Two full channels (Bass, Normal), each two preamp stages with its own Bass/Treble/Volume tone network, mixing at a shared driver bottle ahead of a long-tailed-pair phase inverter and a fixed-bias 5881 pair off a solid-state bridge — no rectifier tube." (at 20 17 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left)) (uuid "d9eb29dc-3bf5-4c4a-88da-c9530f4155dd"))
  (text "The Bass channel's own Treble control sits inside the driver bottle's signal path (V3A -> VR6 -> V3B), not beside its Bass/Volume pots. Heaters, PT primary, ground switch, fuse and standby switch omitted." (at 20 21.5 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left)) (uuid "7e596424-9c46-4d6d-950e-24fa060a2adb"))
